            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0003\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000:F007\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposal fixes a defect in baseline claim C0000 by populating the action and action quote with 'inform', which is directly supported by the statutory text in F007 ('shall immediately inform'). Updating 'shall' to 'must' in the summary accurately reflects the mandatory modal force without altering any conditions, exceptions, or references.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F007\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposal modifies the summary to state that the duty applies unless the entity 'reasonably believes' that the Commission has been adequately informed. F007 explicitly establishes an exception only where the entity has 'actual knowledge' that the Commission has been adequately informed. Substituting an objective reasonable-belief standard for the statutory actual-knowledge standard alters the substantive legal condition.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000:F007\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposal corrects baseline claim C0000 by providing the missing action and action quote ('inform'), directly grounded in F007 ('shall immediately inform'). It retains the accurate summary and preserves all governing scope, conditions, and references.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
